</node>
<node id="Factory Settings">
  <data key="d0">Factory Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Factory Settings are the original state of the device, which can be restored to fix persistent issues that standard troubleshooting cannot resolve.&lt;SEP&gt;Factory Settings refer to the default settings of a device, which can be restored to fix persistent issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Factory Settings refer to the state of a device when it is restored to its original settings, usually to troubleshoot performance issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Factory Settings refers to the state of a device when it is reset to the original configuration as it was at purchase, often used for troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;Factory settings refer to the default settings of the Watch Pro, which can be restored in case of persistent issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af070275f346cb3aabc6679c7791a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcacac32b6b6cffea40cb0a17d301d61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e</data>
