<node id="Phone">
  <data key="d0">Phone</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A phone is a communication device that allows users to make calls, send messages and use various applications including Bluetooth for connecting peripherals.&lt;SEP&gt;Phone refers to a mobile communication device that allows users to make calls, send messages, and access various applications using wireless technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Phone refers to mobile devices enabling communication and application usage.&lt;SEP&gt;The Phone refers to a mobile device used for communication, capable of various functionalities including calling, messaging, and internet access.&lt;SEP&gt;The phone referred to in the document is a mobile device used for communication, multimedia, and various applications, which incorporates features like GPS and internet access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7729ae6048c026d1b7b5e466d0f1c36c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767612065</data>
</node>
<node id="Network Connection">
  <data key="d0">Network Connection</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A network connection refers to the link between devices that allows them to communicate, essential for various functionalities including updates and data synchronization.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Connection encompasses the stability and availability of internet access necessary for app functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Connection refers to the ability of the Nothing Phone to connect to various network types for call and internet services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8dbac70984f20a7113387507b57809f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8</data>
