<node id="Developer Options">
  <data key="d0">Developer Options</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Developer Options are advanced settings on a smartphone that allow users to modify system behaviors, including customizing Bluetooth audio settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Developer Options are advanced settings on devices that allow users to enable features intended for application development and debugging.&lt;SEP&gt;Developer Options are settings within mobile devices that provide developers with advanced features such as USB Debugging and app management tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Developer Options is a set of advanced settings on Android devices, including the Nothing Phone, that allows users to enable features like USB debugging.</data>
