<node id="Active Noise Cancellation">
  <data key="d0">Active Noise Cancellation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a technology designed to reduce unwanted ambient sounds using active noise control mechanisms. This feature is prominently utilized in various audio devices, including CMF Buds 2, Ear (a), Ear (2), and Neckband Pro, aiming to enhance the listening experience for users by blocking out external noise.

In the CMF Buds 2, ANC provides up to 48dB of noise reduction, significantly improving the quality of sound by minimizing distractions from the surrounding environment. Similarly, Ear (a) incorporates ANC to significantly diminish ambient noise, ensuring a better audio experience for its users. The Ear (2) also employs this technology, actively removing external noise up to 40dB, further contributing to a more immersive listening experience.

The Neckband Pro features ANC, which greatly reduces external noise, supporting users in achieving a heightened audio experience. Overall, Active Noise Cancellation is a vital functionality across these devices, allowing users to enjoy their audio without interference from unwanted background sounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767612126</data>
</node>
<node id="Transparency Mode">
  <data key="d0">Transparency Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Transparency Mode is a versatile feature available on various audio devices, including the Neckband Pro and the Ear (1) earbuds. This feature enables users to hear ambient sounds while still enjoying their audio, whether it be music or calls, thereby maintaining a balance between listening and environmental awareness. Specifically, Transparency Mode allows external sounds to pass through the CMF earbuds, ensuring that users remain connected to their surroundings. It enhances situational awareness by permitting the perception of ambient noises, which is particularly beneficial in active environments. Overall, Transparency Mode effectively enriches the listening experience while promoting safety and awareness in users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767612130</data>
</node>
<node id="Everything">
  <data key="d0">Everything</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Everything refers to the overall functioning and interaction of the components and features of the CMF earbuds and the Nothing X app.</data>
