<node id="Gesture Controls">
  <data key="d0">Gesture Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Gesture Controls are touch-sensitive functionalities that enable users to manage various aspects of the CMF earbuds, enhancing usability.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Controls consist of specific actions, such as pressing the earbud's side, to trigger functions on Ear (open), enhancing user interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Controls on Ear (2) allow users to perform various actions like play, pause, and volume adjustment through touch interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Controls refer to the functionality of the Nothing Ear that enables users to perform actions by using touch and swipe on the earbuds, enhancing usability.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture controls allow users to interact with the CMF Earbuds through physical touch on the device's surface, enabling commands like play, pause, and call management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518</data>
