<node id="Dual Connection">
  <data key="d0">Dual Connection</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dual Connection feature is prominently integrated into various models of Nothing Ear, including the Ear (open), Ear (a), and Ear (2). This feature allows the earbuds to connect to multiple devices simultaneously, enhancing user convenience and experience during audio playback and calls. While it facilitates seamless switching between connected devices, users may occasionally experience delays in sound output due to this multi-device capability.

Specifically, the Dual Connection feature enables users to connect their Ear (a) and other Nothing Ear models to two Bluetooth devices at once, allowing for automatic prioritization of connections based on recent activity. This improves overall connectivity options and ensures a smoother audio management experience during calls and media playback. Despite the potential for slight delays, the feature is designed to enhance user interaction with multiple devices effortlessly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8c10ba86f3c652add8c1d23db1a9625b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbcfd0ba7e5f79063be82c76153444e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1887c3e753e5f27cc1105a32465893f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518</data>
