<node id="Environmental Noise Cancellation (ENC)">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Noise Cancellation (ENC)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental Noise Cancellation (ENC) is a sophisticated technology designed to eliminate background noise during phone calls, thereby ensuring clear communication. This feature is utilized across various devices, including the Nothing Ear series, specifically in Ear (a), Ear (2), and Ear (stick) models. ENCs functionality involves enhancing microphone performance by actively reducing ambient sounds, creating a more focused auditory experience for both the speaker and the listener. Additionally, ENC is also implemented in Buds Pro, where it serves a similar purpose of filtering out background noise to maintain the clarity of voice communication. Overall, ENC serves as a vital feature across these devices, promoting clearer conversations by minimizing unwanted distractions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1bc8f3ce2d2c5d835ffeade41737ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700</data>
