<node id="Battery Capacity">
  <data key="d0">Battery Capacity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery capacity is a crucial aspect that defines the power sustainability and lifespan of various devices, including smartphones and wireless earbuds. For mobile phones like the Nothing Phone and its successor, Battery Capacity is quantified at 5000mAh and 4700mAh, respectively, significantly influencing how long the devices can function before needing a recharge. Similarly, the Battery Capacity for the Phone (2a) is also stated to be 5000mAh, highlighting the importance of effective power storage throughout the day.

In the context of earbuds, Battery Capacity plays a vital role in determining usage time. The Buds Pro Earbuds, for instance, have a specific power storage capability that affects how long they can be used between charges. The Nothing Ear earbuds showcase a detailed breakdown of their battery capacity, with each earbud containing 46 mAh and the charging case holding 500 mAh. Furthermore, the Ear (2) specifically has a battery capacity of 33mAh in each earbud and a 485mAh battery in its charging case, allowing for extended usage.

Additionally, the Neckband Pro is noted to have a Battery Capacity rated at 220mAh, dictating its operational duration before requiring a recharge. Overall, Battery Capacity is a defining factor for the performance and usability of these electronic devices, directly impacting their daily operation and user experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9ceda8e99b5757b3aaecad74209f71d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ab8b542ad8bdfa536d2314963d9701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700</data>
