<node id="Airplane Mode">
  <data key="d0">Airplane Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Airplane Mode is a feature that disables all wireless communications on a device, including cellular, Wi-Fi, and Bluetooth connections. This setting is commonly utilized during flights to comply with airline regulations, as well as for troubleshooting calls and connectivity issues. By suspending all wireless transmissions, Airplane Mode can help reset network connections and conserve battery life. On devices such as the Nothing Phone, it serves as a toggle option to ensure that the device does not transmit any signals, providing users with complete control over their wireless functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7e41b65ef7bcc80c8f1decc9bf2928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcacac32b6b6cffea40cb0a17d301d61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2dd4dcddbe486368b957aabc2e335</data>
