<node id="Bluetooth Tethering">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth Tethering</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth Tethering is a method that enables users to share their mobile device's internet connection with other devices via Bluetooth. This technique allows for the wireless sharing of a smartphone's internet connection, providing enhanced connectivity options for various devices. Specifically, Bluetooth Tethering can be utilized with devices such as the Nothing Phone (2), allowing them to access the internet through the phone’s connection. Overall, Bluetooth Tethering serves as a practical solution for users looking to connect multiple devices to the internet using their phone’s capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e55e3fed26fabdb52106695b9582ce3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9025d462a4f9ed5f5840d5850b11449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cecbf41a5540f78302f91235b833c7dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41ebb68d062de192afe8e06b1a67a1c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4524a05ac17de1be9923e9a9dc9c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9ca0a66c298c31fec04cbfc30d7b98c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a</data>
