<node id="Charging Speed">
  <data key="d0">Charging Speed</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Charging speed is the rate at which a mobile phone recharges its battery, which can vary based on the charger used and the device's temperature conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Charging speed refers to the rate at which the Nothing Phone charges, influenced by charger protocols and environmental temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;Charging speed relates to how quickly the Phone 1 can be charged, which varies with temperature and charger protocols.</data>
