<node id="Factory Reset">
  <data key="d0">Factory Reset</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A factory reset is an event or process that restores various devices, including smartphones like the Nothing Phone (1) and smartwatches like the Watch Pro, to their original settings. This process involves erasing all user data and settings, thereby enhancing privacy and security. In doing so, it not only clears all data on the device but also prepares it for troubleshooting or for a new user when changing ownership. Specifically for the Nothing Phone (1), a factory reset erases all user data, ensuring that the device is reverted to its original state. Similarly, the Watch Pro also utilizes a factory reset option to clear all user data and restore the device to its default settings. Overall, a factory reset serves as an important utility for device maintenance and user safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9dbf1c133d4ea12599adde2c8babfb03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76cdae3356bcf4004a71c8e11a80f300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2dd4dcddbe486368b957aabc2e335</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767612309</data>
</node>
<node id="Button">
