<node id="Battery Share">
  <data key="d0">Battery Share</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery Share is a feature that enables devices to wirelessly share their battery power with other compatible devices. This feature enhances usability and connectivity, allowing users to charge one device with another's battery. However, the availability and functionality of Battery Share may vary among different smartphone models. For instance, while many devices support this feature, the Nothing Phone and Phone (2a) do not support Battery Share, limiting its use for users of these specific models. To utilize Battery Share effectively, specific settings must be enabled on devices that do support it, though it is important to note that using this feature can consume the charging device's battery life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3060d71588cf955b2b239dbba0bd791d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af070275f346cb3aabc6679c7791a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b51e206cee412c86265f35f8120e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3de9a6eca983da6478af176236f5152b</data>
