<node id="Glyph Interface">
  <data key="d0">Glyph Interface</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Glyph Interface is a distinctive design feature present on Nothing Phones, particularly notable on the Nothing Phone (1) and Nothing Phone (2). It utilizes light strips located on the back of the devices to deliver visual notifications and alerts, enhancing user interaction through customizable light patterns and sounds for notifications and ringtones. 

The Glyph Interface is characterized by its ability to manage various functions related to notifications, including setting the Bedtime Schedule. Users have the option to tailor their experience by selecting unique light patterns for different notifications and calls, providing a personalized communication method. Though the interface allows extensive customization, it is important to note that it cannot be activated through Google Assistant.

Overall, the Glyph Interface represents an innovative approach to visual display and notification management, creating new interaction methods that effectively enhance communication between the user and the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9025d462a4f9ed5f5840d5850b11449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3060d71588cf955b2b239dbba0bd791d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d37b7781a21f9ace596c3bcb0cbfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af070275f346cb3aabc6679c7791a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cecbf41a5540f78302f91235b833c7dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41ebb68d062de192afe8e06b1a67a1c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9ca0a66c298c31fec04cbfc30d7b98c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0028e301a1da668320afc0e2e78601b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9ff89b42c8123f60ebe4521bfb0cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4524a05ac17de1be9923e9a9dc9c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14c96115117369f38094721a77a31ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34426e6693364728fe244fbfe87a0629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1bc17eaf113f533442b214ae6b6dd</data>
