<node id="eSIM">
  <data key="d0">eSIM</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">eSIM is a digital SIM technology that allows devices to connect to mobile networks without needing a physical SIM card. This feature is available in specific versions of the Nothing Phone, particularly in models sold in Japan, where it enables users to activate cellular plans digitally. However, it is important to note that eSIM is not supported by the Phone (2a), limiting connectivity options for users of that model. The Nothing Phone (3a) does support eSIM technology in the versions sold in Japan, further enhancing the device's capabilities. Overall, eSIM represents a significant advancement in mobile connectivity, providing a more flexible option for users who have compatible devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9ceda8e99b5757b3aaecad74209f71d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ab8b542ad8bdfa536d2314963d9701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cecbf41a5540f78302f91235b833c7dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43c5f3a3b39a02f332e40eef921a1f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41ebb68d062de192afe8e06b1a67a1c4</data>
