<edge source="USB Debugging" target="Nothing Phone">
  <data key="d6">43.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Nothing Phone is equipped with a feature known as USB Debugging, which facilitates advanced connections and troubleshooting with computers. This feature is accessible within the Nothing Phone's settings and is primarily aimed at developers, allowing them to access the device for various programming and operational tasks. USB Debugging is considered essential for executing certain device operations, particularly within developer settings, and provides critical tools for testing and optimizing applications on the device. By enabling USB Debugging, users can unlock enhanced functionality with PCs, making it a necessary step for those engaged in development or technical support for the Nothing Phone.</data>
  <data key="d8">connectivity,developer feature,developer options,developer tools,development,development tool,device management,tech feature,technical feature,technical functionality</data>
